docs {
  # SkyCast API tests (token auth)

  This is a **decoupled** setup: a Laravel JSON API (`/api/*`) authenticated with
  **Sanctum bearer tokens**. The frontend is a separate Vue SPA on :5173.

  How auth works here:

  - `01 Login (admin)` and `12 Login (user)` POST credentials and capture the
    returned `token` into the `token` collection variable.
  - `script:pre-request` (below) attaches `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` to
    every request, so once you've logged in the protected endpoints just work.

  Note: `baseUrl` already includes the `/api` prefix.

  Run order: **01 Login (admin) -> 02..09 (admin) -> 10 Logout -> 11 Register ->
  12 Login (user) -> 13..14 (forbidden checks)**.
}

script:pre-request {
  req.setHeader('Accept', 'application/json');

  const token = bru.getVar('token');
  if (token) {
    req.setHeader('Authorization', 'Bearer ' + token);
  }
}
